  "answer": "**The supplied passages do not establish who must sign the supporting declaration or what that declaration must say about other traders.**\n\n**Manual practice — supporting declarations:** The Manual directs that, where a declaration is required, it should conform with regulations 21.6 and 21.7. Those Regulations are not supplied, so I cannot identify the required signatory or declaration contents from this material. The Manual also reports that, under regulation 21.4, a document requiring a supporting declaration may be treated as not filed until that declaration is provided. These are statements from the Manual, not supplied legislative text. [TMM/Part2/3/2/3/6]\n\n**Manual practice — other traders:** The supplied section 41 guidance concerns opposition particulars, not a supporting declaration for an application. It requires brief reasons why other traders, acting without improper motive, are likely to want to use the mark; merely asserting that desire without explaining why is inadequate. It does not establish that an applicant’s supporting declaration must contain that statement. [TMM/Part47/1/1/2/5~1]\n\n**Legislation:** None of the supplied Act passages answers these declaration questions. The relevant Regulations would be needed to confirm the requirements."
